user.js
*.mp3
# Compiled bytecode is a build artefact, not source: a committed .pyc ships a binary and
# looks runnable to a reviewer while being impossible to review.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# A checkout used as the prefix puts his config, his conversations, the socket token and his
# speech inside the tree: none of that is source, and the token least of all. The bridge writes
# beside its own `server.py`, so for the normal layout that is `face/`; a root copy is covered
# too. `face/web/presets.json` is the shipped preset library and must stay tracked, which is why
# these are exact paths rather than a glob.
/config.json
/history.json
/token
/audio/
/*.json.tmp
face/config.json
face/history.json
face/token
face/theme-sync-off
face/audio/
